        }
      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "summary",
          "text": "An update for kernel is now available for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.2 Extended Update Support.\n\nRed Hat Product Security has rated this update as having a security impact of Important. A Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE link(s) in the References section.",
          "title": "Topic"
        },
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: tcp: restrict SO_ATTACH_FILTER to priv users (CVE-2026-53236)\n\n* kernel: fuse: re-lock request before replacing page cache folio (CVE-2026-53388)\n\n* kernel: net: shaper: rework the VALID marking (again) (CVE-2026-64027)\n\n* kernel: net/handshake: hand off the pinned file reference to accept_doit (CVE-2026-63979)\n\n* kernel: net/handshake: Drain pending requests at net namespace exit (CVE-2026-63978)\n\n* kernel: af_unix: Fix UAF read of tail->len in unix_stream_data_wait() (CVE-2026-64109)\n\n* kernel: net/handshake: Take a long-lived file reference at submit (CVE-2026-64523)\n\n* kernel: net: gro: fix double aggregation of flush-marked skbs (CVE-2026-68136)\n\n* kernel: net/packet: avoid fanout hook re-registration after unregister (CVE-2026-68338)\n\n* kernel: scsi: target: core: Fix iSCSI ISID use-after-free in REGISTER AND MOVE (CVE-2026-72083)\n\n* kernel: KVM: s390: pci: Reject adapter interrupt forwarding if already enabled (CVE-2026-74515)\n\n* kernel: net: smc: fix splice entry lifetime imbalance in smc_rx_splice (CVE-2026-74631)\n\n* kernel: usb: usbfs: fix use-after-free of usb_device in usbdev_release() (CVE-2026-80824)\n\n* kernel: smb: client: clear setuid/setgid bit on write with cifsacl/modefromsid/posix extensions (CVE-2026-89638)\n\n* kernel: vfio/pci: clear vdev->msi_perm after freeing it on init failure (CVE-2026-89777)\n\n* kernel: md/raid5-ppl: fix use-after-free in ppl_do_flush() (CVE-2026-93262)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* x86/microcode: Add platform mask to Intel microcode \"old\" list [RHEL-10] [rhel-10.2.z] (JIRA:RHEL-212778)\n\n* net: NULL pointer deref kernel panic in fib6_walk_continue under heavy VRF churn [rhel-10.2.z] (JIRA:RHEL-245489)\n\n* backport fixes for lockdep issues reported with rt-debug [rhel-10.2.z] (JIRA:RHEL-259937)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
          "title": "Details"
        },
