        "title": "kernel: net/handshake: hand off the pinned file reference to accept_doit"
      },
      {
        "cve": "CVE-2026-64027",
        "cwe": {
          "id": "CWE-416",
          "name": "Use After Free"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-07-19T00:00:00+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2502341"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the `net/shaper` component of the Linux kernel. A race condition exists in how `VALID` marks are handled for entries in an XArray. This can lead to a Use-After-Free (UAF) vulnerability, where memory is incorrectly freed while still in use, potentially allowing an attacker to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "kernel: net: shaper: rework the VALID marking (again)",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This vulnerability is rated as Moderate impact for Red Hat Enterprise Linux because exploitation requires local access with network configuration capabilities, and successful exploitation depends on winning a complex race condition. Under specific timing windows during network shaper updates, an uncoordinated table modification can trigger kernel memory corruption leading to a system crash. The affected traffic shaping framework is relatively new and not utilized in typical default deployment profiles, restricting the scope of affected enterprise environments.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
