          "name": "Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-08-10T00:00:00+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2513264"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the Linux kernel's `net/packet` subsystem. A race condition can occur during the re-registration of a fanout hook after a network device has been unregistered. This issue arises when the `packet_set_ring()` function attempts to re-add a fanout hook based on a stale state, potentially leading to an inconsistent system state and a denial of service (DoS).",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "kernel: net/packet: avoid fanout hook re-registration after unregister",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
