            "category": "workaround",
            "details": "To mitigate this flaw on hosts that do not operate as storage target servers, prevent the LIO target kernel modules from loading:\n\n1. Create a configuration file to prevent loading the target modules:\n# echo \"install iscsi_target_mod /bin/true\" > /etc/modprobe.d/disable-iscsi_target.conf\n# echo \"install target_core_mod /bin/true\" > /etc/modprobe.d/disable-target_core.conf\n\n2. Stop the SCSI target daemon if active:\n# systemctl stop target.service\n\nWarning: Modifying kernel module loading or stopping target.service requires a service restart or system reboot, and will immediately interrupt active storage connections on systems acting as storage targets.\n\nIf the machine must function as an iSCSI target, use network firewall rules to restrict access to the iSCSI target port (TCP port 3260) strictly to authorized initiator hosts.",
