          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the Linux kernel. A local attacker can cause a Denial of Service (DoS) or potentially escalate privileges through a use-after-free vulnerability in the RAID-5 Partial Parity Log (PPL) component. During flush operations, the system improperly continues to access an input/output (I/O) tracking structure after it has already been released. This memory corruption can destabilize the operating system and cause the kernel to crash.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "kernel: md/raid5-ppl: fix use-after-free in ppl_do_flush()",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
